{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_17","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -c \"cd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_20-38-28-etcd_raft-real-run/draft && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport json\np='submission.json'\nd=json.load(open(p))\nd['sources']=[\n {'id':'switch_to_config','file':'raft.go','start_line':1975,'end_line':2030,'kind':'code_observation'},\n {'id':'leader_propose_drop','file':'raft.go','start_line':1290,'end_line':1295,'kind':'code_observation'},\n {'id':'tick_heartbeat','file':'raft.go','start_line':862,'end_line':889,'kind':'code_observation'},\n {'id':'send_heartbeat','file':'raft.go','start_line':692,'end_line':707,'kind':'code_observation'},\n]\nd['investigations']=[{\n 'ref':'@removed_leader_stall',\n 'question':'When a committed configuration change removes the current leader and Config.StepDownOnRemoval is false, does the cluster still reach a new leader, or does the ineligible leader keep the leadership role and its heartbeats reset every eligible voter so that no proposal can commit and no election can complete without external intervention?',\n 'source_ids':['switch_to_config','leader_propose_drop','tick_heartbeat','send_heartbeat'],\n 'hypothesis':'switchToConfig keeps the leadership role for a node that is absent from the new configuration when step-down is not requested, stepLeader then drops every proposal because the leader has no progress entry, and tickHeartbeat keeps broadcasting heartbeats that reset every remaining voter\\\\'s election timer, so the cluster can neither commit client writes nor elect a replacement; with StepDownOnRemoval=true the same applied change makes the node a follower and the remaining voters elect a new leader.',\n 'discriminator':'Propose, replicate and apply a ConfChangeV2 that removes node 1 on a three-voter cluster, then tick every node for a fixed number of rounds with prompt message delivery and record node states, whether a new leader was elected, the last index and committed index, and the proposal errors on the leader and on a forwarding follower; repeat with StepDownOnRemoval=true as the control. Also probe the read path on the ineligible leader with one and then a quorum of acknowledgments from the current voters. If the ineligible leader is eventually replaced, or if the followers campaign despite the heartbeats, the hypothesis is refuted.',\n 'disposition':'active',\n 'limitations':[\n  'The harness drives timers by ticking each node once per round in a fixed order, which is a legitimate but synthetic schedule; a real deployment also has network and scheduling jitter.',\n  'The probe covers simple removal of the leader in a three-voter cluster; joint configurations, learner demotion and multi-node changes are not exercised.',\n  'Whether StepDownOnRemoval=false is the right default for an embedding service, and whether an operator is expected to intervene, is a contract question outside the captured package.'\n ]\n}]\njson.dump(d,open(p,'w'),indent=2)\nprint('ok', list(d.keys()))\nPY\ncd /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance && timeout 120 .venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-11_20-38-28-etcd_raft-real-run --submission submission.json; echo \\\"EXIT=\"'$?\"'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
